{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"228c8af25374e90f212d97e699be3c83c986b1935858cb09c769636957f315b7","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_50abaaf7526abf941f5afb6bd3ffdc1b74a9e4af3b8561ae7e917cdb93d4dfcb","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a method for visualizing deep neural network decisions by extending the prediction difference analysis with conditional sampling, multivariate patch analysis, and hidden-layer visualization. The contribution is primarily methodological, offering a probabilistically grounded approach to instance-specific saliency that distinguishes evidence for and against a class. The work is positioned against existing gradient-based and occlusion-based methods, with experiments on ImageNet and medical MRI data demonstrating the utility of the proposed improvements.","paper_id":"BJ5UeU9xx","paper_identity_sha256":"71aa7f99d53134984c5af4e5f84fc6c78812de02d413e2bca0b8486746c6a6c5","prompt_identity_sha256":"6be496581565b6f796aa49d3162e0d992430df770e47c612e31636cdfe7decbb","raw_response_sha256":"315e7edf86cb27a10c84829759f70b76316bd854d9f8a317f2c269da7cf9135c","request_identity_sha256":"e1e40f3740e42a1515602b7bcef0f5fb47f16c6068cd46a2530e299f9777450b","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"ORIG","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"c071e1fec98a3a3d9bdca635e35adfca0f291ee0e34954f1cd6390ded4d5a3b7","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-003","SRC-004"],"review_text":"The paper does not introduce a fundamentally new problem or task, as instance-specific visualization of neural network decisions is an established area of research. The authors position their work within the existing landscape of saliency map generation, specifically addressing the need for a 'probabilistically sound methodology' to explain classification decisions. While the application to medical imaging is highlighted as a domain of interest, the core problem formulation remains consistent with prior work on interpreting black-box classifiers.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-PROB"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-015"],"review_text":"The methodology is an extension of the prediction difference analysis by Robnik-Sikonja and Kononenko (2008). The authors claim three substantial improvements: conditional sampling, which replaces the crude marginal distribution approximation with a neighborhood-based conditional; multivariate analysis, which removes patches of pixels rather than single features to account for network robustness; and deep visualization, which adapts the method to analyze hidden layers. These modifications are presented as necessary to make the method tractable and effective for high-dimensional data like images and deep networks.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-MTH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-023","SRC-024"],"review_text":"The paper provides insights into the behavior of deep networks by distinguishing between evidence for and against a class, which is not always apparent in standard saliency maps. The analysis of hidden layers reveals how different network depths specialize in features, such as edge detectors in early layers and higher-level features in middle layers. The comparison between penultimate and output layer visualizations offers insight into how the softmax operation influences the interpretation of class-specific evidence, showing that the output layer captures the decision boundary between similar classes more distinctly.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-ANL"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-026","SRC-027"],"review_text":"The experimental setup utilizes standard benchmarks (ImageNet) and a specific medical dataset (COBRA) for MRI scans. The evaluation protocol involves comparing the proposed method against marginal sampling and logistic regression weights. While the use of the COBRA dataset for medical imaging is a specific application, the experimental design primarily serves to demonstrate the method's applicability rather than introducing a new benchmark or evaluation protocol for interpretability. The computational cost is noted as a limitation, with analysis times ranging from 20 to 70 minutes per image depending on the network.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-012","SRC-013"],"review_text":"The paper combines the probabilistic framework of prediction difference analysis with image-specific priors, such as local neighborhood dependencies and patch-based feature removal. The rationale for this combination is that the original univariate and marginal approaches are insufficient for high-dimensional, correlated data like images. The combination is presented as a way to make the probabilistic explanation more accurate and computationally feasible for deep learning models.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-COM"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-028"],"review_text":"The paper includes a comparison with logistic regression weights in the medical imaging context, noting that the proposed method produces less noisy and more input-specific visualizations. However, this is a comparative evaluation rather than a systematic negative result or critical assessment of the limitations of existing methods. The paper does not present a dedicated section on negative results or a rigorous analysis of failure cases for the proposed method.","subdimension_id":"ORIG-NEG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"8f3f41139666d5ef606346456f6d3bac0e05127bb028bc402c060b8ef4cb1b3f","paper_id":"BJ5UeU9xx","paper_ordinal":20,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"315e7edf86cb27a10c84829759f70b76316bd854d9f8a317f2c269da7cf9135c","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJ5UeU9xx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"4301f7c9fb263820c4d973d34877c6567c57aa8767350852b2833fefbded43a4","request_identity_sha256":"e1e40f3740e42a1515602b7bcef0f5fb47f16c6068cd46a2530e299f9777450b","role":"ORIG","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1082,"prompt_tokens":18136,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19218},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"e1e40f3740e42a1515602b7bcef0f5fb47f16c6068cd46a2530e299f9777450b","role":"ORIG","role_ordinal":3,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}